  {
   "name": "mart_data_quality",
   "rows": 7,
   "grain": [
    "issue_order"
   ],
   "description": "The defects that exist in the source drops and survive into the warehouse as flags rather than deletions. Publishing it is the point: a dashboard that quietly drops the rows it cannot reconcile is how a practice ends up believing a number that is short.",
   "columns": [
    {
     "name": "issue_order",
     "type": "INTEGER"
    },
    {
     "name": "issue",
     "type": "VARCHAR",
     "values": [
      "Appointment status captured in mixed case",
      "Appointment status that did not map to a known state",
      "Claim submitted more than once by the switch",
      "Dates exported as DD/MM/YYYY instead of ISO",
      "Diagnosis code missing on the encounter",
      "Payment quotes an appointment that does not exist",
      "Site name captured in more than one spelling"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "source_table",
     "type": "VARCHAR",
     "values": [
      "Appointments",
      "Claims",
      "Claims and sessions",
      "Clinics",
      "Encounters",
      "Patient payments"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "treatment",
     "type": "VARCHAR",
     "description": "What was done about it, in words a practice manager can check.",
     "values": [
      "Deduplicated on claim id in silver. Counting both would double the denied value and overstate the headline.",
      "Folded to one spelling for display. Nothing joins on the name, so this affects labels rather than numbers.",
      "Mapped explicitly through a lookup rather than title cased, so a value nobody expected becomes null and fails a test instead of quietly becoming a fourth status.",
      "Parsed by a macro that handles both. Left to a default cast, roughly one date in four would land null or in the wrong month.",
      "Row kept and flagged, excluded from anything attributed to a site. The money is real, the visit it belongs to is not in the file.",
      "Row kept and flagged. A missing ICD-10 is one of the reasons a claim comes back, so these are counted rather than filled in.",
      "The test above, expressed as a count. It is zero, and it is published anyway: a quality panel that only lists the failures cannot tell you what was checked."
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "rows_affected",
     "type": "BIGINT"
    },
    {
     "name": "impact_zar",
     "type": "DOUBLE"
    },
    {
     "name": "is_present",
     "type": "BOOLEAN"
    }
   ]
  },
